\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Object-conditioned cross-channel reconfiguration architecture. Color frames acquired at 15 fps are processed asynchronously; the nominal 200-Hz supervisor polls the bounded latest-result queue without waiting for inference. The first threshold-qualified mapped class triggers one strategy event $\Theta (c)$, which updates the enabled slave-impedance, haptic-interface, and gripper settings and is then locked for the trial. No result or confidence below 0.25 retains the initial state, whereas a detected but unmapped class invokes the balanced default strategy. Green paths show asynchronous perception and one-shot updates; the blue loop shows continuous human teleoperation and force/state feedback. Five-mode channel-update logic and comparison roles are given in Table~\ref {tab:3}.}}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:3}{{3}{8}{}{figure.3}{}}
